I have just made a modification to nethack (3.0j).  This modification
automatically opens doors when you run into them.

Why make this modification?

1 - When you run into a hostile monster, you do the most sensible thing
    and attack it with your weapon in hand.  IMHO, it would make sense 
    to do the most sensible thing when you run into a door -- open it.

2 - I'm used to playing an old version of nethack without doors.  I'm
    getting tired of always having to press 'o' to open them.

I'd like some people to try this out and let me know what they think.
If everyone seems to like it, I may submit this to the nethack gods
for inclusion in a future release.

Before I submit it, I will make it more robust (currently I just 
cloned a section of code from lock.c into hack.c -- ideally both 
of these would use the same procedure, called something like
opendoor(x,y) ), and I may try to make it an option you could turn 
off and on.  This is just a quick and dirty implementation to try
it out.

Limitations: It only works if you are in line with the door (not
diagonally).  It does not work if you are blind, stunned, have
dexterity < 10, or are fumbling.  It also does not work if the 
door is locked.  I'm not sure if I should remove some of these
limitations -- particularly the dex<10 one.


